# A kitten left hungry runs off; one that was only put away does not; another's kitten nearby is not ours.
# Facts (OSRS wiki, Kitten): very hungry 3 minutes after "hungry", gone 3 minutes after that; a new
# kitten from Gertrude costs 100 coins. Lines from the wiki's Transcript:Kitten. Ids: RuneLite gameval
# NpcID.KITTENPET_BLACK, NpcID.KITTENPET_LIGHT. The follower is stood in for by "follower" (ReplayTest).
include /replays/scenes/varrock.scene
watch tier plaque.shown.tier
watch why plaque.shown.why
watch gone kitten.gone
watch out kitten.out
npc KITTENPET_BLACK "Kitten" 3204 3432 as kitten
# Someone else's kitten close by is never taken for the player's.
npc KITTENPET_LIGHT "Kitten" 3202 3432 as stranger
tick 5
expect out = false
expect title = null
follower KITTENPET_BLACK
tick 5
expect out = true

# Hungry, then very hungry: going to waste, the last minutes counting down.
chat GAMEMESSAGE "Your kitten is hungry."
tick 300
chat GAMEMESSAGE "Your kitten is very hungry."
tick 5
expect title = "Feed your kitten"
expect tier = WASTING
expect why ~ "It is very hungry: it runs off in about 3 min unless fed"
# Its time runs out and it is gone from beside the player, not into the pack: it ran off.
tick 300
remove kitten
follower none
tick 15
expect gone = "ran off"
expect title = null
